    "body": "preview refresh already dry-runs the visual span at every extra cursor, and that is how the other cursors get the right `in` after `an`. but `vim.treesitter._select` keeps one module-level history of which child `select_parent` came from. the last extra cursor therefore overwrites that history, and the primary's next `in` actually lands on the first child.\n\nso each preview refresh now ends with one more dry-run of the same span at the primary's own session start. shared lua state is hence last written for the primary, as if the other cursors' replays had not run.\n\nFixes #42000",
    "closed_at": "2026-09-21T20:56:19Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "the `ubuntu release gcc functionaltest` fail is `swapfile_preserve_recover_spec.lua` (#22096), not the mcursor change. the treesitter selection tests passed on that job, and the other functionaltest jobs are green. i can't re-run the job from the fork. can someone kick that one?",
